hive 0.0.1  — run any command with no/invalid args for its full usage

Usage
  hive <command> [args]

Spawn & run
  hive spawn <bee>                              start bees in detached tmux sessions (--frame to spawn a swarm)
  hive template <list|run|define|…>             manage and run reusable single-bee spawn presets
  hive new                                      interactive picker: choose type, account, config & folder, then spawn
  hive run <bee> -p <prompt>                    spawn, send a prompt, optionally wait and clean up
  hive x <bee> <prompt>                         spawn a bee and hand it a prompt, then return (fire-and-forget)
  hive xa <bee>                                 spawn a bee and attach to it
  hive open <bee>                               registered spawn presented where you are (link window or attach)

Message
  hive send <selector> <prompt>                 send a prompt to a bee, swarm, or colony
  hive answer <bee> [text]                      answer a blocked HSR bee's needs-input (default: yes)
  hive brief <selector> <text>                  send a one-time context brief
  hive buz <send|inbox|read|…>                  addressed messaging: four-tier delivery + per-bee policy
  hive task <add|ls|done|…>                     shared micro-task lists with gated auto-supply (task supply <bee> --on)
  hive track <define|attach|status|…>           expected step sequences attached to one bee
  hive rename <selector> <title>                set a bee's display title (--here for current bee, --auto to derive one, --clear)
  hive tag <selector> <tag>...                  add/remove user tags on bees (--remove, --list)
  hive seal <selector> --from <p>               record a typed handoff artifact

Observe
  hive list                                     show all known sessions with state (alias: ps)
  hive state <ls|explain>                       BeeView read model: display state, requests, results, freshness (--json)
  hive bees                                     grouped fuzzy fleet TUI; --json emits one authoritative snapshot and exits
  hive fleet [<bee>|--all]                      orchestrator fleet trees with live state + seals (no arg: self inside a bee, else all fleets; --all forces all; --json)
  hive gateways                                 list operator gateway advertisements and liveness
  hive tail <session>                           capture or follow pane content
  hive transcript <session>                     render structured transcript rows
  hive last <session>                           print the bee's most recent assistant message or seal
  hive wait <session>                           block until the bee goes idle or seals
  hive search <query>                           search seals, ledger, and session records (seals find: seals only)
  hive events                                   tail the ledger's event stream (--follow, --type <glob>, --session <bee>, --since 15m, --json)
  hive usage [<account>]                        progress against providers' real 5h/weekly limits (--live dashboard; alias: limits)
  hive spend <ingest|report|leverage|…>         local API-equivalent cost ledger + subscription leverage from transcripts

Manage bees
  hive attach <session>                         attach to the tmux session (nesting-safe inside tmux)
  hive next                                     jump to the next bee needing you (needs-auth/needs-reply/needs-action/stop-failed/ready; --prev, --state)
  hive fork <bee> [checkpoint]                  branch a bee's thread into a fresh bee (--at <turn>, --list-anchors)
  hive handoff <bee> [-p <instr>]               compact via self-seal and start a fresh bee from the summary (--from-seal)
  hive here                                     resolve the bee owning the current pane (--id, --json)
  hive spawn-picker [--frame|--flow]            print frame/flow names for a display-popup spawn chord
  hive urls [<bee>]                             list URLs printed in a bee's pane (--lines, --open, --json)
  hive keys <print|path|check>                  print/verify the recommended tmux keybinding set
  hive retire <bee|@swarm|colony:name>          stop a bee and archive its record (the everyday way to end bees; alias: archive)
  hive kill <session>                           PURGE a bee: stop it and delete its record/seals/run data (rare; prompts, --yes)
  hive promote <bee>                            move an HSR bee onto an interactive tmux pane (resume; codex/grok/opencode/kimi, --now)
  hive set-model <bee> <model>                  change a bee's model in place, resuming its session (--clear, --fresh, --now, -- <harness flags>)
  hive demote <bee>                             move a tmux bee back to a pane-less HSR runner (resume; codex/grok/opencode/kimi, --now)
  hive revive <bee>                             relaunch a dead bee and resume its session (--crashed, --all, --fresh, --session <id>, --no-wait)
  hive auth-resume <bee>                        reuse valid disk credentials (or require login), resume, and replay the failed prompt
  hive clean --dead|--crashed|--idle|-i         remove dead/crashed metadata, kill idle bees, or clean interactively
  hive loop <launch|start|status|stop|…>        run a bee repeatedly until a stop condition (launch = interactive dialog)
  hive flight <start|status|ls|sweep|…>         fixed-capacity worker flights: slot leases, seal contracts, deterministic replacement

Organize
  hive colony <list|create|…>                   manage project-scoped namespaces
  hive pool <list|status|spawn|…>               checkout pools: claim clean pro clones round-robin (also: spawn --pool)
  hive swarm <list|inspect|destroy>             manage live or destroyed bee cohorts
  hive frame <list|define|…>                    manage reusable swarm blueprints
  hive flow <list|run|runs|…>                   manage and run flow definitions
  hive comb <define|run|runs|…>                 manage immutable combs and durable graph runs
  hive own <owner> <bee>...                     set the owned-by/reports-to edge (--clear to unset)
  hive move <bee> --colony <c>                  reassign a bee's colony (or --owner <o> alias)

Accounts
  hive account <list|add|sync|…>                manage provider accounts in the local credential vault
  hive activate <account>                       seed an account's credentials into a home slot (fast login)
  hive login <account>                          interactive (re)login seat in tmux; captures fresh credentials
  hive swap-account <bee> <account>             re-credential a bee's home and resume on another account
  hive cell-cred mint <account> --harness <k>   mint a short-lived ephemeral credential and print it as JSON on stdout

Substrate & daemon
  hive execution repair-lease-archive <bee>     inspect/apply one proof-bound historical execution lease archive correction
  hive node <list|register|…>                   manage substrate endpoints (local + ssh-tmux)
  hive substrate list                           show available substrate kinds
  hive daemon <status|logs|…>                   manage the hive daemon LaunchAgent + inspect state/logs
  hive deploy [<sha>]                           versioned deploy to ~/.hive/runtime + daemon restart (--rollback, --list, --init)
  hive sessions reconcile                       index sessions across all homes; flag dupes and conflicts
  hive sync manifest                            write the syncthing include/exclude manifest

Setup
  hive config <show|set-bee|…>                  view or edit ~/.hive/config.json defaults
  hive completion <bash|zsh|fish>               print a shell completion script (eval to install)

Bees
  claude, codex, opencode, grok, kimi, pi, droid, cursor — or any executable on PATH
  home aliases: codex1, codex2, codex3, cc1, cc2, cc3
  account shorthands: <tool>-<account fragment> (codex-ur, claude-thto) — see hive account list
  <tool>-auto / --account auto: pick the least-loaded account (pace-aware: prefers unused quota expiring at the next reset)

Env overrides
  HIVE_CLAUDE_CMD="claude --model sonnet" hive spawn claude
  HIVE_CODEX_YOLO=1 hive spawn codex
  HIVE_CODEX_START_CONCURRENCY=2 hive x codex "task"  — bounded HSR cold starts; 0 disables
  HIVE_DEBUG_SPAWN=1 hive spawn claude  — print a per-phase spawn timing breakdown to stderr
  hive spawn codex2 · hive spawn claude --home ~/.claude-3 · hive spawn cc3

